-- A place's names follow one rule now: `ko` the Korean spelling most used,
-- `en` the name a label prints, neither with an appellation tag (나파 밸리,
-- not 나파 밸리 AVA), and every other spelling in use among the synonyms
-- (Burgundy, Tuscany, 버건디, 충주, Niigata Prefecture ...). Places that
-- collected bottle data named but the tree lacked are added (villages, grand
-- crus, states, Korean 시·군). Keys stay, so no bottle changes. The rows are
-- the dictionary's projection, rendered from catalog/dictionary/places.json.

